Description: manage system-wide Node.js versions via NVM and update-alternatives
 update-node-alternative combines the NVM infrastructure (used to download
 and store Node.js binaries under /usr/local/share/nvm/versions/node/) with
 Debian's update-alternatives mechanism (used to switch the /usr/local/bin/
 symlinks for node, npm, npx and corepack).
 .
 It is designed in the spirit of update-java-alternatives(8) and honours
 the DEBIAN_FRONTEND convention from debconf(7): supported frontends are
 dialog (whiptail/dialog), readline, gnome (zenity), kde (kdialog) and
 noninteractive, with a sensible auto-detection when DEBIAN_FRONTEND is
 unset. The tool supports installing, removing, listing (local and
 remote) Node.js versions, switching the active version, and migrating
 npm global packages between versions.
